# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Licensed assets — NEVER commit. See §9 of the implementation plan.
# FLAME is non-commercial research use and non-redistributable; NoW is research
# use; the texture space is CC BY-NC-SA. Committing any of these, even to a
# private repo, is redistribution. This section is a licence control, not tidiness.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.tar
*.pkl
*.npz
FLAME20*/
TextureSpace/
NoW_Dataset/
scans/
scans_lmks_onlypp/
imagepaths*.txt
deca_model*
FLAME_albedo_from_BFM*
mediapipe_landmark_embedding/
models/
landmark_embedding*

# The synthetic CI fixture contains no MPI data and is the one model we may ship.
!tests/fixtures/tiny_head.pkl

# Third-party checkout; pinned by URL in the README rather than vendored.
now_evaluation-main/

# DECA reference checkout, kept for comparison. Non-commercial research licence
# that forbids redistribution, so it is never committed.
reference/

# Demo photographs — consent is per-image and tracked separately.
data/photos/

# FFHQ: CC BY-NC-SA as a collection, and 6.5 GB besides. The ingest is
# reproducible from scripts/data/ingest_ffhq.py, so only the recipe is tracked.
data/ffhq/

# DigiFace-1M: R-UDA v1.0, redistribution requires binding recipients to the
# same terms. The ingest recipe is tracked; the data is not.
data/digiface/

# Arc2Face: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Derived from WebFace42M, i.e. scraped source
# images -- the licence covers the authors' restoration work, not the
# provenance of what it restored. Never redistribute; the ingest reads it
# remotely and only the recipe is tracked.
data/arc2face/

# CelebA crops written by scripts/data/ingest_celeba.py -- 161k files, and the same
# no-redistribution terms as the cache below. Listed separately because the
# cache rule alone left these visible to `git add -A`, which then spent minutes
# trying to stage 12 GB of licence-restricted images.
data/celeba/

# CelebA, pulled as parquet by scripts/eval/diag_corpus_identity.py. The release
# agreement is explicit: non-commercial research only, and "you agree not to
# further copy, publish or distribute any portion". Copies are permitted for
# internal use at a single site, which is what this cache is. The face
# identities are formally request-gated; this mirror ships them.
data/_hfcache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
out/
*.obj
# Exported heads, anywhere. A GLB carries FLAME's template and topology, and
# every checkpoint so far was trained against FLAME 2020, whose licence forbids
# redistribution. Committing one to a public repo is the thing that licence is
# about. Safe to commit only once the pipeline is retrained on FLAME 2023 Open
# (CC-BY-4.0, attribution required).
*.glb
*.gltf
runs/
checkpoints/
*.log

